{
  "id": "availability-heuristic",
  "term": "availability heuristic",
  "definition": "The availability heuristic is a mental shortcut in which people judge how common or likely something is by how easily examples come to mind. It can bias judgment because information that is more retrievable may be treated as more frequent or probable than it really is.",
